<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n382" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγγᾰρος</span></b> , ὁ, in
		Persia, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>mounted courier</i>, for
			carrying royal dispatches, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.126
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				8.6.17
			</span></i>, Theopomp. Hist. <i><span class="en">
				106
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> term of
			abuse ( 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φορτηγός</span>
			)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ἄ. ὄλεθρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					2
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				<u>Or.</u>
				1.129
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
			Adj., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. πῦρ</span> the
				<i>courier</i> flame, of beacon fires, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				282
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. ἡμίονοι</span>
			<i>posting-mules</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				<u>Or.</u>
				18.143
			</span></i>. (Assyr. <i>agarru</i>, 'hired labourer'.)</div>
